From: x6100-q3 <x6100-q3@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: btusb: keep events ahead of held ACL data

With poll_sync, ACL data that arrives before the HCI event it depends on
is held back until the next event or one polling interval. Two gaps let
it through early anyway:

- btusb_recv_event() woke rx_work before passing the event to the core,
  so on SMP the worker could deliver the held data first;
- the hold time was intr_interval jiffies, and a delay of one jiffy may
  expire at the very next tick, i.e. almost at once with HZ=100/250.

On the Xiegu X6100 (RTL8723BU, Wi-Fi and Bluetooth on one USB device
behind a musb host) this made LE pairing fail at random: SMP key
distribution arrived before Encryption Change and was dropped. Pass the
event first and hold data for one jiffy more than the interval.

---
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c	2026-10-25 22:56:53
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c	2026-10-25 22:56:53
@@ -1221,12 +1221,20 @@
 
 static int btusb_recv_event(struct btusb_data *data, struct sk_buff *skb)
 {
+	int err;
+
+	/* Hand the event to the core before releasing the ACL data held
+	 * back behind it: woken first, rx_work can run on another CPU and
+	 * deliver that data ahead of the event it was waiting for.
+	 */
+	err = data->recv_event(data->hdev, skb);
+
 	if (data->intr_interval) {
 		/* Trigger dequeue immediately if an event is received */
 		schedule_delayed_work(&data->rx_work, 0);
 	}
 
-	return data->recv_event(data->hdev, skb);
+	return err;
 }
 
 static int btusb_recv_intr(struct btusb_data *data, void *buffer, int count)
@@ -1306,7 +1314,10 @@
 		return data->recv_acl(data->hdev, skb);
 
 	skb_queue_tail(&data->acl_q, skb);
-	schedule_delayed_work(&data->rx_work, data->intr_interval);
+	/* One jiffy more than the interval: a delay of N jiffies may expire
+	 * at the very next tick, i.e. after less than one polling interval.
+	 */
+	schedule_delayed_work(&data->rx_work, data->intr_interval + 1);
 
 	return 0;
 }
